          "lean": "optional",
          "standard": "required",
          "enterprise": "required"
        },
        "note": "One product outcome at the root (never a business outcome or traction metric); opportunities in the customer's voice, citing snapshots or feedback items; a target opportunity chosen by comparing siblings. lean (when the user has heard from customers): a short ranked opportunity list, not a tree. standard: the full tree with about three solutions and assumption tests. enterprise: one tree per product outcome under opportunity-solution-trees/, opportunities tagged by segment or tenant role, tests tracked. Versioned per discovery cycle (opportunity-solution-tree)."
      },
